Based on Sophisticated Backpacks and Sophisticated Core
--------------------------------------------------------

AlleviatedBackpacks is an unofficial Bedrock adaptation of Sophisticated Backpacks 3.23.4 and
Sophisticated Core 1.2.9 by P3pp3rF1y
(https://github.com/P3pp3rF1y/SophisticatedBackpacks commit cf55d7d6,
https://github.com/P3pp3rF1y/SophisticatedCore commit 3690ed29), the last versions released under
GPL-3.0. Parts of its logic are adapted from that source code and are used under GPL-3.0. Later
All-Rights-Reserved versions are not used.

Sophisticated Backpacks and Sophisticated Core: Copyright (C) P3pp3rF1y, licensed under GPL-3.0
(the versions named above).

Modifications
-------------

- Reimplemented in C++ as a LeviLamina native mod for Minecraft Bedrock Edition (server and
  client); no Java source file is included. The logic adapted from SB / SC is rewritten for
  Bedrock's APIs, data formats and UI.
- Textures and icons are original pixel art generated by tools/textures/*.ps1 and
  tools/models/backpack.ps1. The 3D model is Bedrock geometry written for this project; its box
  layout follows SB 3.23.4's backpack block models and renderers, used under GPL-3.0.
- Features that SB / SC added after the versions above are not included (among them the Alchemy
  and Mob Catcher upgrades, the Ender Linker and linked storage, backpack templates and the Stack
  Upgrade conversion items). Java-only mod integrations are left out.
- Bedrock-specific additions and changes (Hopper upgrades, client companion screens, energy and
  fluid API, LevelDB storage, the /backpack command); see docs/FEATURES.md for the full comparison.
- Language texts: texts taken from SB / SC come from the en_us / zh_cn files of the versions named
  above and are used under GPL-3.0 (later SB / SC releases also state that translations "are freely
  available with no license restrictions"). Texts those versions do not have, in either language,
  are our own. In-game texts are in English and Simplified Chinese.

